cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "IKAT: anchor-preserving ingestion for figure-grounded RAG"
message: "If you use this software or its measurements, please cite the paper in paper/."
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.2.0
abstract: >-
  Layout parsers emit an ordered block sequence in which a figure's position
  states where it belongs. Conventional ingestion discards that ordering and
  reconstructs placement from captions. IKAT preserves the reading-order anchor
  at ingestion instead, and composes a vision-language filter with a
  cross-encoder ranker for selection.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - multimodal retrieval
  - document layout analysis
  - figure grounding
